cifs: Pass a pointer to virt_to_page() in cifsglob

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author Linus Walleij <linus.walleij@linaro.org>
commit 605a97e8398af21ba8ea6e6f3ffe069e09e24277
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/605a97e8.failed

Like the other calls in this function virt_to_page() expects
a pointer, not an integer.

However since many architectures implement virt_to_pfn() as
a macro, this function becomes polymorphic and accepts both a
(unsigned long) and a (void *).

Fix this up with an explicit cast.

	Acked-by: Tom Talpey <tom@talpey.com>
	Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij <linus.walleij@linaro.org>
(cherry picked from commit 605a97e8398af21ba8ea6e6f3ffe069e09e24277)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

